{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     post/body — the article body, and the decision about its layout.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ WHY THIS IS A BRANCH AND NOT A CONDITIONAL <aside>.

     `.ns-post` is a THREE-COLUMN grid: a 14rem aside, the prose measure, and
     a 3.5rem rail. Grid places children by source order, so a `.ns-post` with
     one child puts the article in the FIRST column — 14rem wide. The page
     does not look like it is missing an aside; it looks like the body is
     broken, and the cause is two elements away from the symptom.

     So the column count has to be chosen at the same moment as the contents,
     and NSDS already ships the variant for it: `--wide` is the single-column
     form. The layout decision therefore cannot live inside the TOC partial —
     it has to happen out here, before either is emitted.

     The cost is that `{{> "post/prose"}}` appears four times. That is why it
     is a partial: the branch duplicates one line, not the article markup.

     ── The control, in precedence order ───────────────────────────────────
       #no-toc / #no-sidebar   full width, no rail
       #toc                    rail, whatever the site setting says
       neither                 the `show_toc` setting decides

     Per-post tags beat the site setting because a publisher sets a default
     and an author overrides it for one page — which is the only ordering
     that makes both controls useful.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{#has tag="#no-toc, #no-sidebar"}}
    <div class="ns-post ns-post--wide">{{> "post/prose"}}</div>
{{else has tag="#toc"}}
    <div class="ns-post">{{> "post/toc-aside"}}{{> "post/prose"}}</div>
{{else}}
    {{#if @custom.show_toc}}
        <div class="ns-post">{{> "post/toc-aside"}}{{> "post/prose"}}</div>
    {{else}}
        <div class="ns-post ns-post--wide">{{> "post/prose"}}</div>
    {{/if}}
{{/has}}

{{#if tags}}
    <div class="ns-page ns-page--prose">
        <ul class="ns-taglist">
            {{#foreach tags}}<li><a class="ns-tag" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a></li>{{/foreach}}
        </ul>
    </div>
{{/if}}
